es. Order is another cube, that's going to be my answer. This order takes care of the neighbors for actions or nodes in a cube. As long as the cube is not empty, we're going to pop it. And then we're going to append that current node that is just being popped from the cube into order. Now it comes the second loop that we've spent because BFS we're going to expand. Now we have the current node, we're going to explore their kits or neighbors for a graph. Once we visit their neighbors, what we'll do is that we're going to reduce their indegrees by one because the current node is already investigated into order, that means it happens, it's being executed, it's ordered. And if that number now is down to zero, that means they're free to be executed right next. So we're going to add that to the cube. And I believe that's it, that's the end of the algorithm, we're going to return order, which is the list of execution after we traverse all the nodes that started with zero degree or later got reduced to zero degree, they will be executed in order in that order cube. But we're going to make sure if the size of the order is the same size of the sheer amount of a stages, otherwise there will be a cycle and we're going to return an empty list.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 4.12, "text": " Okay, let me first read out the problem.", "tokens": [50364, 1033, 11, 718, 385, 700, 1401, 484, 264, 1154, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.39576074188830807, "compression_ratio": 1.3655172413793104, "no_speech_prob": 0.18026769161224365}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 4.12, "end": 16.16, "text": " It's a speech pipeline problem, DAG, a direct async, a cycle graph.", "tokens": [50570, 467, 311, 257, 6218, 15517, 1154, 11, 9578, 38, 11, 257, 2047, 382, 34015, 11, 257, 6586, 4295, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.39576074188830807, "compression_ratio": 1.3655172413793104, "no_speech_prob": 0.18026769161224365}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "sta